p = "experiments/E320_soft-attach-replaces-snap/experiment.md"
s = open(p, encoding="utf-8").read()
def rep(old, new):
    global s
    assert s.count(old) == 1, (old[:70], s.count(old))
    s = s.replace(old, new)

# S4: the attached end is not guaranteed to be a delivered piece end
rep('''The end = w0 x keypoint + sum w_m x node_m, the heading the normalised weighted mean, so the curve starts / ends ON a node of B when the weight is concentrated and falls back to the keypoint when nothing is in reach.''', '''The end = w0 x keypoint + sum w_m x node_m, the heading the normalised weighted mean: a convex combination of the keypoint and the candidate nodes, so it lies on a node only when one weight dominates, and it falls back to the keypoint when nothing is in reach. **It is not guaranteed to be a delivered piece end** (amendment): the candidates are the raw nodes with existence above 0.05 including mid-section nodes of a lane, the weighted mean lies inside their hull, the dustbin falls back to the keypoint, and the 4 m / 45 degree wiring of the read-out still decides which pieces the connector is joined to.''')
rep('''the pieces are wired by the default rule of `add_connectors` (every delivered piece end within 4 m / 45 degrees of the connector end, the E284 / E287 way), so a connector that is attached to a node of B touches the pieces that start / end at that node.''', '''the pieces are wired by the default rule of `add_connectors` (every delivered piece end within 4 m / 45 degrees of the connector end, the E284 / E287 way), so a connector whose end lies near a node of B is joined to the pieces that start / end within that reach (the proximity rule decides the edges, not the attachment).''')
rep('''pair recall / precision (unchanged by construction: the pair logits do not see the attachment),''', '''pair recall / precision against E312 of the same seed (NOT unchanged: the pair logits do not see the attachment, but the tokens, the maps head and the scale head are trained jointly with the geometry loss and the cross entropy, so they can move),''')
# S5 + S7: more report items
rep('''Reported next to it: lanes found, maneuver coverage''', '''Reported next to it (amendment, S5 / S7): `curves`, `wired_both_ends` and the number of long links of B that the connectors cover and drop, attach against unsnapped against snapped (`ends_card_*thr0.1.json`; under `--attach` the cover test of `qends_eval.add_connectors` for the long links uses the ATTACHED ends too, a second change next to the geometry of the curve: said here so that a difference in lanes found or duplicates is not blamed on the attachment alone); the attached-end error against the GT end on the VAL dump next to the keypoint error (`jdiag.py kperr e320_a_s<S> e312_p_s<S>` prints both, strict one-to-one match, p >= 0.5; the train-frame numbers `att_acc`, `att_kp_d`, `geom_end_d` of the log include the GT-injected keypoints, whose error is about 0.65 m, and are NOT VAL claims); lanes found, maneuver coverage''')
# S3: attribution paragraph before "Two seeds, VAL 873 frames"
rep('''Two seeds, VAL 873 frames, TEST untouched. **Prediction (a number):** topo F1 of arm a is 0.005 below''', '''**Attribution (amendment, S3).** Arm a carries `--geom-w 0.5`; the controls c and u (the stored E312 runs) do not. A KEEP therefore says that the RECIPE (geometry loss + attachment + the attached read-out) replaces the snap, not that the attachment alone did. E317 predicts about +0.015 topo F1 on the unsnapped read-out from the geometry loss alone, so the clause "above u + 0.02" can be met with almost no help from `Attach`. The missing reference is E317 arm g (the same recipe without `--attach`) read out unsnapped: it is held by D85 and has not been run; if E320 is a KEEP the follow-up card runs it (or E320 gets a run without `--attach`, `--geom-w 0.5` only) so that the share of the attachment is measured, before any claim that "the attachment replaces the snap". The ranking of the two read-outs of arm a itself (attached against unsnapped of the SAME run, `score` without `--attach`) is reported as the within-run effect of the attached ends.
Two seeds, VAL 873 frames, TEST untouched. **Prediction (a number):** topo F1 of arm a is 0.005 below''')
rep('''attachment accuracy `att_acc` of the training log above 0.8 at the end; the attached end error `geom_end_d` below the keypoint error `att_kp_d`.''', '''attachment accuracy `att_acc` of the training log above 0.8 at the end; the attached end error `geom_end_d` below the keypoint error `att_kp_d` (train frames with GT-injected keypoints, not VAL claims; the VAL claim is the `jdiag.py kperr` line). The prediction is close to a coin flip against the KEEP bound (0.005 above it).''')
# S8: no watcher
rep('''Reported next to it (amendment, S5 / S7)''', '''**The kill criterion is not enforced during the run** (amendment, S8): there is no watcher for "`att_ce` below 1.0 at step 1000"; the run is NOT stopped early, the criterion is read from `train.log` afterwards, and a run that meets it is reported as CUT-by-kill with its numbers (the same for the keypoint F1 of the maps and for a non-finite loss, which the trainer's own roll-back guard handles). Reported next to it (amendment, S5 / S7)''')
# tests list
rep('''self-tests of `jends_eval.py`, `qends_eval.py`, `jmaneuver.py` and the real `jends_train.py --help`.''', '''self-tests of `jends_eval.py`, `qends_eval.py`, `jmaneuver.py` and the real `jends_train.py --help`. After the critic pass (amendment): a `--geom-w > 0` batch without `ppts` raises, `score --attach` without `--thr` writes `ends_card_attach_thr0.5.json` and leaves `ends_card.json` alone, `jdiag.py kperr` prints the attached-end error for a dump that has `att_pos`.''')
